title: Walter Gropius
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

German architect.

Founded the [[BauHaus]] in Weimar in 1919 and ran it until 1928. Designed its building in Dessau.

His idea was one school for all the arts, with craft and workshop at the center and building as the goal.

Later taught at Harvard.

See [[Educational Model]], [[Modernism]], [[The Preliminary Course]]
